1
00:00:00,420 --> 00:00:02,879
On Isru Chag, our yeshiva had yeshiva on

2
00:00:02,879 --> 00:00:04,519
Isru Chag and I was taking attendance in

3
00:00:04,519 --> 00:00:07,139
the 11th-grade class on Isru Chag and I

4
00:00:07,139 --> 00:00:09,000
knew that two of the boys in the

5
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:11,320
class had gone to Eretz Yisrael for Yom

6
00:00:11,320 --> 00:00:13,439
Tov and yet I had perfect attendance in

7
00:00:13,439 --> 00:00:14,839
the class on Isru Chag. So I asked

8
00:00:14,839 --> 00:00:15,720
one of the boys, \"How did you get

9
00:00:15,720 --> 00:00:17,620
back so fast?\" And he said, \"Well, I

10
00:00:17,620 --> 00:00:19,420
landed at 5 o'clock this morning and came

11
00:00:19,420 --> 00:00:21,940
straight to yeshiva. That's pretty good. Asked the

12
00:00:21,940 --> 00:00:22,940
other boy, \"How did you get back so

13
00:00:23,300 --> 00:00:25,539
fast?\" Said, \"Landed 9 o'clock last night.\" \"So

14
00:00:25,539 --> 00:00:27,149
when did you leave Eretz Yisrael? \"Left Eretz

15
00:00:27,149 --> 00:00:29,760
Yisrael on Yom Tov Sheni shel Galuyos. So

16
00:00:29,760 --> 00:00:32,000
he said the whole plane was full of

17
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:33,700
Jews from the Five Towns, from Teaneck, from

18
00:00:33,700 --> 00:00:36,200
Queens, whatever, who were in Eretz Yisrael and

19
00:00:36,200 --> 00:00:38,000
keep one day of Yom Tov in Eretz

20
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:40,240
Yisrael and flew back on Yom Tov Sheni

21
00:00:40,240 --> 00:00:42,179
shel Galuyos because for them it wasn't Yom

22
00:00:42,179 --> 00:00:44,259
Tov. So I was it got me thinking

23
00:00:44,259 --> 00:00:46,539
about this issue, and someone had sent me

24
00:00:46,539 --> 00:00:48,320
an email also asking me about this issue,

25
00:00:48,320 --> 00:00:50,439
so I started to think about: is this

26
00:00:50,439 --> 00:00:52,740
something that's permissible? Someone who's keeping one day

27
00:00:52,740 --> 00:00:54,600
of Yom Tov in Eretz Yisrael and wants

28
00:00:54,600 --> 00:00:56,700
to fly back on Yom Tov Sheni shel

29
00:00:56,700 --> 00:00:58,719
Galuyos, is that permissible to do? It seems

30
00:00:58,719 --> 00:01:00,679
to be that the hamon am has paskened

31
00:01:00,679 --> 00:01:02,140
that it is, but we have to see

32
00:01:02,140 --> 00:01:04,659
what the halacha has to say about it.

33
00:01:04,659 --> 00:01:07,319
So in order to understand this topic, you

34
00:01:07,319 --> 00:01:09,060
first need to understand a little bit about

35
00:01:09,060 --> 00:01:10,853
what it means to be a ben Chutz

36
00:01:10,853 --> 00:01:12,319
La'aretz in Eretz Yisrael and how many days

37
00:01:12,319 --> 00:01:13,859
of Yom Tov one is supposed to keep

38
00:01:13,859 --> 00:01:16,159
when they're a ben Chutz La'aretz in Eretz

39
00:01:16,159 --> 00:01:20,099
Yisrael. And there are basically three opinions about

40
00:01:20,099 --> 00:01:21,939
a ben Chutz La'aretz who's in Eretz Yisrael.

41
00:01:21,939 --> 00:01:24,700
Most poskim, the majority of poskim seem to

42
00:01:24,700 --> 00:01:27,140
assume that you keep two days, and it's

43
00:01:27,140 --> 00:01:29,219
really based on a mishna Maseches Pesachim that

44
00:01:29,219 --> 00:01:31,420
you take upon yourself the chumros of the

45
00:01:31,420 --> 00:01:33,200
makom that you went to and the place

46
00:01:33,200 --> 00:01:35,159
that you came from, and since you're coming

47
00:01:35,159 --> 00:01:37,099
from a place that keeps two days, so

48
00:01:37,099 --> 00:01:39,439
you maintain those chumros and you keep two

49
00:01:39,439 --> 00:01:41,480
days even when you're in Eretz Yisrael if

50
00:01:41,480 --> 00:01:43,420
you are a ben Chutz La'aretz, if you

51
00:01:43,420 --> 00:01:45,579
are someone who lives in Chutz La'aretz. However,

52
00:01:45,719 --> 00:01:49,420
there is a much-celebrated and publicized shita of

53
00:01:49,420 --> 00:01:51,439
the Chacham Tzvi. The Chacham Tzvi wrote a

54
00:01:51,439 --> 00:01:57,200
teshuva where he holds, in the teshuva is

55
00:01:58,879 --> 00:02:01,640
in Siman kuf-samech-zayin, where the Chacham Tzvi writes:

56
00:02:01,640 --> 00:02:05,471
Nireh l'aniyus da'ati d'tzrichim heima l'hisnaheig b'inyanei hamoadim

57
00:02:05,471 --> 00:02:09,304
k'echad mibnei Eretz Yisrael hatoshvim v'ein zeh bikhlal

58
00:02:09,304 --> 00:02:12,060
chumrei makom sheyatza misham, that a person would

59
00:02:12,060 --> 00:02:13,860
keep one day if they're in Eretz Yisrael.

60
00:02:13,860 --> 00:02:16,199
This does not get included in the general

61
00:02:16,199 --> 00:02:18,280
rule of keeping the chumros of the place

62
00:02:18,280 --> 00:02:20,419
that you came from because this is a

63
00:02:20,419 --> 00:02:24,039
place-oriented thing; this is about the place. So

64
00:02:24,039 --> 00:02:25,379
of all of the bnei Chutz La'aretz who

65
00:02:25,379 --> 00:02:26,740
come to Eretz Yisrael, obviously they would be

66
00:02:26,740 --> 00:02:29,939
they would keep only only one day. He

67
00:02:31,039 --> 00:02:33,251
writes: V'ein beyad anshei Eretz Yisrael l'hosif yom

68
00:02:33,251 --> 00:02:35,344
echad yoser mehakasuv baTorah l'hachmir af haba miChutz

69
00:02:35,344 --> 00:02:37,438
La'aretz asur mehem linhog sheni Yom Tov shel

70
00:02:37,438 --> 00:02:39,680
Galuyos. Not only are they allowed to keep

71
00:02:39,680 --> 00:02:42,520
one day, they must keep one day. They're

72
00:02:42,520 --> 00:02:45,180
not allowed to keep a second day of

73
00:02:45,180 --> 00:02:47,039
Yom Tov. That is the shita of the

74
00:02:47,039 --> 00:02:49,599
Chacham Tzvi. The majority of poskim did not

75
00:02:49,599 --> 00:02:51,319
hold like the Chacham Tzvi. Rav Schachter likes

76
00:02:51,319 --> 00:02:52,860
to point out that it seems that the

77
00:02:52,860 --> 00:02:56,360
Chacham Tzvi has become more popular amongst poskim

78
00:02:56,360 --> 00:02:59,199
in recent times, but that's the shita of

79
00:02:59,199 --> 00:03:01,120
the Chacham Tzvi. It's important to realize if

80
00:03:01,120 --> 00:03:03,039
you hold like the Chacham Tzvi, it comes

81
00:03:03,039 --> 00:03:05,139
out a major chumra for bnei Eretz Yisrael

82
00:03:05,139 --> 00:03:08,870
that when bnei Eretz Yisrael go to Chutz

83
00:03:08,870 --> 00:03:11,699
La'aretz, so they have to then observe like

84
00:03:11,699 --> 00:03:13,800
bnei Chutz La'aretz; they have to observe two

85
00:03:13,800 --> 00:03:15,439
days of Yom Tov and would not be

86
00:03:15,439 --> 00:03:17,259
allowed to keep one day of Yom Tov.

87
00:03:17,259 --> 00:03:20,340
But generally, people don't apply the Chacham Tzvi

88
00:03:20,340 --> 00:03:21,840
that way; they like to apply the Chacham

89
00:03:21,840 --> 00:03:23,806
Tzvi in the other direction when bnei Chutz

90
00:03:23,806 --> 00:03:24,979
La'aretz go to Eretz Yisrael to keep only

91
00:03:24,979 --> 00:03:26,960
one day. And then there's a third approach,

92
00:03:26,960 --> 00:03:28,219
or I guess you'd call it a third

93
00:03:28,219 --> 00:03:31,300
and a fourth approach, with Rav Soloveitchik and

94
00:03:31,300 --> 00:03:34,020
the talmidei Rav Soloveitchik have have an approach

95
00:03:34,020 --> 00:03:37,180
where they essentially say Rav Soloveitchik said that

96
00:03:37,180 --> 00:03:39,360
really me'ikar hadin he thinks we should pasken

97
00:03:39,360 --> 00:03:41,439
like the Chacham Tzvi, that the Chacham Tzvi

98
00:03:41,439 --> 00:03:42,879
is really correct and really we should only

99
00:03:42,879 --> 00:03:45,120
keep one day. But because there's such a

100
00:03:45,120 --> 00:03:48,139
significant amount of poskim that hold that you're

101
00:03:48,139 --> 00:03:49,860
supposed to keep two days, so he thought

102
00:03:49,860 --> 00:03:52,340
that we should respect those poskim by being

103
00:03:52,340 --> 00:03:56,500
machmir for for two days. And that's what

104
00:03:56,500 --> 00:04:00,319
they call the day and a half. It

105
00:04:00,319 --> 00:04:01,800
doesn't actually mean a day and a half,

106
00:04:01,800 --> 00:04:04,219
obviously, but it means that you should be

107
00:04:04,219 --> 00:04:07,170
extra machmir. So essentially you follow the Chacham

108
00:04:07,170 --> 00:04:08,580
Tzvi, you davon a tefillas chol on the

109
00:04:08,580 --> 00:04:09,819
second day, you put on tefillin with a

110
00:04:09,819 --> 00:04:11,280
bracha on the second day, but as a

111
00:04:11,280 --> 00:04:12,860
way of compromise, you don't do any melacha

112
00:04:12,860 --> 00:04:14,680
on the second day to be choshesh for

113
00:04:14,680 --> 00:04:16,579
those that say two days. That was Rav

114
00:04:17,079 --> 00:04:18,920
Soloveitchik's. Rav Schachter thinks the opposite way. Rav

115
00:04:18,920 --> 00:04:20,920
Schachter thinks that the majority of poskim in

116
00:04:20,920 --> 00:04:22,699
the me'ikar hadin is that you're really supposed

117
00:04:22,699 --> 00:04:24,879
to keep two days of Yom Tov. So

118
00:04:24,879 --> 00:04:26,839
that's always been the the majority. So you

119
00:04:26,839 --> 00:04:28,500
don't do melacha on the second day, you

120
00:04:28,500 --> 00:04:30,800
davon a tefillas Yom Tov because it's Yom

121
00:04:30,800 --> 00:04:33,620
Tov, you say kiddush, you you do a

122
00:04:33,620 --> 00:04:35,579
second seder, but at the same time you

123
00:04:35,579 --> 00:04:38,060
have to be choshesh that maybe it's really

124
00:04:38,060 --> 00:04:40,180
only one day, and therefore you should put

125
00:04:40,180 --> 00:04:41,560
on tefillin on the second day without a

126
00:04:41,560 --> 00:04:44,259
bracha, you should listen to havdala at the

127
00:04:44,259 --> 00:04:46,300
end of the first day to make sure

128
00:04:46,300 --> 00:04:49,060
that you're being yotzei for those shitos that

129
00:04:49,060 --> 00:04:50,879
hold one day. So that's what people sometimes

130
00:04:50,879 --> 00:04:52,639
call two and a half days, which also

131
00:04:52,639 --> 00:04:54,180
doesn't mean anything; it doesn't mean two and

132
00:04:54,180 --> 00:04:55,779
a half days, it means that to be

133
00:04:55,779 --> 00:04:57,860
choshesh in that way. So those are the

134
00:04:57,860 --> 00:05:00,519
three basic approaches. Most poskim seem... Two days,

135
00:05:00,519 --> 00:05:03,040
Chacham Tzvi says one day, and then there's

136
00:05:03,040 --> 00:05:07,540
various permutations of compromise or being extra machmir.

137
00:05:07,540 --> 00:05:09,819
One day me'ikar hadin with a chumra of

138
00:05:09,819 --> 00:05:11,959
two days or two days me'ikar hadin with

139
00:05:11,959 --> 00:05:14,279
a chumra of one day. Rav Schachter just

140
00:05:14,279 --> 00:05:15,839
added a wrinkle to this and he has

141
00:05:15,839 --> 00:05:19,279
this very great chidush that he holds that

142
00:05:19,279 --> 00:05:21,740
if you're part of a group and the

143
00:05:21,740 --> 00:05:24,600
majority of that group is holding one shittah,

144
00:05:24,600 --> 00:05:27,319
then the entire group is bound to that

145
00:05:27,319 --> 00:05:29,139
shittah. So for example, he said he was

146
00:05:29,139 --> 00:05:30,899
asked a case of a girl who had

147
00:05:30,899 --> 00:05:32,899
studied in a seminary in Israel and now

148
00:05:32,899 --> 00:05:34,540
she was back home and all of her

149
00:05:34,540 --> 00:05:36,156
teachers in seminary told her that when a

150
00:05:36,156 --> 00:05:37,879
ben chutz la'aretz comes to Eretz Yisrael like

151
00:05:37,879 --> 00:05:39,600
Rav Moshe, like Rav Shlomo Zalman, like everyone

152
00:05:39,600 --> 00:05:42,139
holds, she should keep two days, but her

153
00:05:42,139 --> 00:05:44,060
parents and the rest of her family where

154
00:05:44,060 --> 00:05:45,160
they were going to go for yom tov

155
00:05:45,160 --> 00:05:46,879
now and they were going to keep one

156
00:05:46,879 --> 00:05:48,680
day. So she wanted to know what should

157
00:05:48,680 --> 00:05:50,199
she do? Should she keep two days because

158
00:05:50,199 --> 00:05:52,339
that's what her rabbeim told her or should

159
00:05:52,339 --> 00:05:53,660
she keep one day? So he said well

160
00:05:53,660 --> 00:05:55,579
if your whole family is keeping one day

161
00:05:55,579 --> 00:05:56,980
then you should keep one day because it's

162
00:05:56,980 --> 00:06:00,319
a violation of lo sisgodedu to break up

163
00:06:00,319 --> 00:06:01,939
in a single group to have people doing

164
00:06:01,939 --> 00:06:04,319
some people doing one thing and other people

165
00:06:04,319 --> 00:06:07,519
doing something else. Now Rav Schachter thought there

166
00:06:07,519 --> 00:06:09,279
was a rabbi from California that was coming

167
00:06:09,279 --> 00:06:11,720
with a large group of families from his

168
00:06:11,720 --> 00:06:13,699
shul and he said bechol mikreh no matter

169
00:06:13,699 --> 00:06:15,160
what I tell them, the majority of them

170
00:06:15,160 --> 00:06:17,120
are going to keep one day anyway. So

171
00:06:17,120 --> 00:06:19,000
what should the rest of them do? So

172
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:22,279
he thought also lo sisgodedu would determine that

173
00:06:22,279 --> 00:06:23,920
if you're all in the same situation and

174
00:06:23,920 --> 00:06:26,819
most of that group is following a reliable

175
00:06:26,819 --> 00:06:29,540
shittah like the Chacham Tzvi to keep one

176
00:06:29,540 --> 00:06:31,660
day, so then the whole group should keep

177
00:06:31,660 --> 00:06:33,519
one day even though Rav Schachter holds me'ikar

178
00:06:33,519 --> 00:06:36,120
hadin really it should be two days, but

179
00:06:36,120 --> 00:06:38,560
lo sisgodedu would trump that. He has pointed

180
00:06:38,560 --> 00:06:40,000
out to me that that's only if everyone

181
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:42,540
is in the same circumstance. What if not

182
00:06:42,540 --> 00:06:44,439
everyone is in the same circumstance? Some of

183
00:06:44,439 --> 00:06:45,740
the people in your group are there for

184
00:06:45,740 --> 00:06:47,439
all three regalim. Some of the people in

185
00:06:47,439 --> 00:06:49,199
your group own an apartment there. Some of

186
00:06:49,199 --> 00:06:50,980
the people but you're in the same group

187
00:06:50,980 --> 00:06:53,500
but everyone has different circumstances, so he didn't

188
00:06:53,500 --> 00:06:54,959
think that that would be a violation of

189
00:06:54,959 --> 00:06:57,160
lo sisgodedu for everyone to do their own

190
00:06:57,160 --> 00:07:00,180
thing in that situation. But the real tricky

191
00:07:00,180 --> 00:07:03,519
question is what defines a ben Eretz Yisrael?

192
00:07:03,519 --> 00:07:05,839
Let's say you want to hold like the

193
00:07:05,839 --> 00:07:07,879
rov poskim that a ben chutz la'aretz in

194
00:07:07,879 --> 00:07:10,379
Eretz Yisrael keeps two days. But how do

195
00:07:10,379 --> 00:07:11,846
you know if you are a ben chutz

196
00:07:11,846 --> 00:07:14,139
la'aretz or a ben Eretz Yisrael? What is

197
00:07:14,139 --> 00:07:16,620
the geder? So the pashtus is one would

198
00:07:16,620 --> 00:07:19,040
imagine that it should depend on the majority

199
00:07:19,040 --> 00:07:20,899
of the time spent. If you spend the

200
00:07:20,899 --> 00:07:23,019
majority of your year in chutz la'aretz, you're

201
00:07:23,019 --> 00:07:25,240
a ben chutz la'aretz. Or for example when

202
00:07:25,240 --> 00:07:26,959
someone asks, hey where do you live? So

203
00:07:26,959 --> 00:07:28,300
do you say I live in Eretz Yisrael,

204
00:07:28,300 --> 00:07:29,579
do you say I live in chutz la'aretz?

205
00:07:29,639 --> 00:07:33,339
So if that's where you koveia yourself, that's

206
00:07:33,339 --> 00:07:35,560
where you consider yourself to live, pashtus is

207
00:07:35,560 --> 00:07:37,500
that would be the koveia, that would be

208
00:07:37,500 --> 00:07:39,579
the geder. But not everyone agrees with that.

209
00:07:39,579 --> 00:07:42,439
Rav Shlomo Zalman Auerbach and Rav Soloveitchik both

210
00:07:42,439 --> 00:07:44,879
held that if you are three regalim in

211
00:07:44,879 --> 00:07:46,800
Eretz Yisrael, if a person stays in Eretz

212
00:07:46,800 --> 00:07:49,220
Yisrael for all three regalim every year, and

213
00:07:49,220 --> 00:07:51,699
not just Succos and Pesach because they're long

214
00:07:51,699 --> 00:07:54,720
regalim, but really all three regalim, Shavuos included,

215
00:07:54,720 --> 00:07:56,920
so then a person's always there for three

216
00:07:56,920 --> 00:07:59,160
regalim, since this is a yom tov'dike din,

217
00:07:59,160 --> 00:08:01,199
this is about yom tov, so if a

218
00:08:01,199 --> 00:08:02,860
person's there for three regalim, that makes him

219
00:08:02,860 --> 00:08:05,120
a ben Eretz Yisrael l'gabbei this and therefore

220
00:08:05,120 --> 00:08:07,476
he can keep one day. That's how Rav

221
00:08:07,476 --> 00:08:09,220
Soloveitchik held. The Gerer Rebbe had a chidush

222
00:08:09,220 --> 00:08:10,920
that if you own an apartment, if you

223
00:08:10,920 --> 00:08:13,740
own a dirah in Eretz Yisrael, so then

224
00:08:13,740 --> 00:08:16,360
you can call yourself a ben Eretz Yisrael.

225
00:08:16,360 --> 00:08:18,579
I saw in Piskei Teshuvos he points out

226
00:08:18,579 --> 00:08:20,720
that someone who's half half, who's not really

227
00:08:20,980 --> 00:08:22,439
sure, lives half of his time in Eretz

228
00:08:22,439 --> 00:08:23,319
Yisrael, half of his time in chutz la'aretz,

229
00:08:23,519 --> 00:08:25,236
spends a number of regalim in Eretz Yisrael,

230
00:08:25,236 --> 00:08:28,259
some sometimes in chutz la'aretz, has businesses in

231
00:08:28,259 --> 00:08:31,019
both places, he's really, could go either way,

232
00:08:31,019 --> 00:08:33,960
so yesh omrim she'azlinan achar makom shenimtza sham

233
00:08:33,960 --> 00:08:35,480
yoser, some say well you gotta figure out

234
00:08:35,480 --> 00:08:37,340
which place are you there more often, but

235
00:08:37,340 --> 00:08:41,120
others, he quotes other poskim that disagree, he

236
00:08:41,120 --> 00:08:43,879
quotes the Shevet HaLevi and the Zekan Aharon

237
00:08:43,879 --> 00:08:46,320
and some others that disagree and say that

238
00:08:46,320 --> 00:08:49,480
you would go with wherever you happen to

239
00:08:49,480 --> 00:08:51,399
be. So if you happen to be in

240
00:08:51,399 --> 00:08:52,700
Eretz Yisrael for that yom tov, you'd keep

241
00:08:52,700 --> 00:08:53,820
one day, if you happen to be in

